&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hyperscale Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; An understanding of how &quot;The Big Five&quot; and other CSPs operate—including their procurement cycles and large-scale deployment hurdles—is a significant plus. Experience with server ODM / rack integrators is also a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Management &amp;amp; Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working together with these functions&amp;nbsp; is vital. You must be able to track long-tail projects with dependencies (e.g., NPI phases, product lifecycles). A background in Ops or Program Management is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRM Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced proficiency in Salesforce (SFDC). You should be comfortable managing complex data sets and understanding how sales data impacts manufacturing forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong analytical skills are required to track and manage demand, supply, and other key business metrics, and to synthesize key information for internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Building: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to develop strong relationships across a diverse personas at varied seniority levels, including procurement, engineering, quality, operations, and product management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
