&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Finance Business Partner for Technology &amp;amp; Growth, you will serve as the primary Finance partner to Everpure&#39;s newly established Technology and Growth Organization, led by our Chief Technology and Growth Officer. This highly visible role will help shape the financial strategy behind new products and business models while owning the planning and operating rhythm for a broad, evolving organization. You will partner directly with senior leaders across Technology and Growth, Digital Transformation and the CIO organization, Enterprise and Commercial Lines of Business, the EXA product business unit, and Corporate Development. This is also a build opportunity: you will establish and lead a Finance team and operating model designed to scale with the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the financial strategy for new and evolving business models within EXA and the broader Technology and Growth Organization, developing pricing, demand, and financial models that evaluate subscription, consumption, licensing, hybrid, and other emerging commercial constructs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic Finance partner to the Chief Technology and Growth Officer and senior leaders across Digital Transformation, the CIO organization, Enterprise and Commercial Lines of Business, EXA, and Corporate Development, bringing a clear financial point of view to strategic, operating, and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end planning, budgeting, and forecasting across headcount, opex, and capex, leading annual operating plans and rolling forecasts while ensuring alignment with company-wide planning priorities and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex financial and operational performance into executive-level reporting, insights, and recommendations that inform resource allocation, business priorities, and long-term growth decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Corporate Development and business leaders to evaluate new opportunities, strategic investments, transactions, and complex commercial arrangements, clearly modeling financial implications, risks, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the Finance team and operating model supporting the organization, while driving the automation, standardization, and system improvements needed to scale forecasting, reporting, and decision support.&lt;/li&gt;
