&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure is seeking a full-time Embedded Firmware Simulation Engineer to join our device firmware team. You will be responsible for developing high-fidelity virtual platforms that abstract complex hardware behaviors to accelerate SSD firmware development. In this role, you will be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining comprehensive firmware simulation environments (e.g., QEMU) to enable shift-left testing, reducing dependency on physical hardware and accelerating time-to-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating accurate, high-fidelity hardware models to abstract controller logic, communication interfaces (PCIe, NVMe), and NAND media behaviors within Pure Storage’s DirectFlash™ SSD Modules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing instrumentation tools to profile performance and analyze failures within the simulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automating CI/CD pipelines to seamlessly integrate simulation and virtual platforms into our firmware release and validation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering closely with ASIC vendors to validate firmware behaviors against RTL and digital logic designs before physical silicon is available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and scaling high-fidelity simulation software for complex embedded, firmware, or hardware-software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level proficiency in C/C++ and Python for both firmware and modeling development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with simulation/emulation tools and methodologies (e.g., QEMU, SystemC, TLM, or instruction-set simulators).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of firmware-hardware interaction, including the ability to translate complex schematics and data sheets into abstract software models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of high-performance storage protocols such as PCIe and NVMe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded software development, SoC bring-up, and RTOS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SoC, or hardware bring-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good verbal communication &amp;amp; collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing and able to work onsite in an open office and team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
