&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driven by curiosity and a passion for solving complex system challenges? As a Hardware Validation Engineer in our Hyperscale Line of Business (HLOB) Hardware team, you will serve as the critical bridge between core hardware engineering and real-world customer deployments. You will bring up, test, and troubleshoot dynamic server platforms, shaping the reliability of next-generation infrastructure. Working closely with cross-functional software, firmware, and customer-facing teams, you’ll directly impact system stability and platform readiness. If you thrive on methodical problem-solving at the intersection of hardware, Linux, and system architecture, this role offers an exceptional platform to expand your technical impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Platform Bring-Up &amp;amp; System Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead end-to-end bring-up and testing for diverse server platforms and hardware configurations, ensuring robust system reliability before customer deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execute Root-Cause Analysis &amp;amp; Technical Diagnostics:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform deep-dive troubleshooting across hardware, firmware, and Linux system layers to isolate complex failures and deliver actionable engineering recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate &amp;amp; Optimize Validation Workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and maintain custom shell scripts and diagnostic tools to streamline testing processes, improve coverage, and accelerate issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Cross-Functionally for Deployment Success:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate directly with internal Hardware, firmware, software, test development teams and external customer and partner teams to resolve technical roadblocks and continuously elevate platform performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems &amp;amp; Validation Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience in server validation, system bring-up, lab engineering, or hardware testing environments is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linux Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on command of Linux environments—including installation, system configuration, command-line usage, and failure diagnosis using standard tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; A structured approach to debugging unfamiliar system behaviors across hardware, OS, and firmware interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scripting &amp;amp; Automation Capabilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical skill in writing and using Bash, Python, or other shell scripts to automate diagnostics and workflow tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong verbal and written communication skills to document complex diagnostic findings and partner effectively across global engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
