&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure is seeking a Senior Product Manager to help shape and execute the market strategy for systems offerings across mid-market, SMB, and adjacent commercial segments. This role sits within the Commercial Line of Business Product Portfolio team and partners closely with Inbound PMs, Central Hardware PMs, and cross-functional leaders across Sales, Marketing, Finance, Supply Chain, Customer Experience, Engineering, and Operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is designed for a product manager who can connect customer insight, competitive dynamics, positioning, packaging, and launch execution to drive high-impact commercial outcomes. The ideal candidate brings strong systems and hardware fluency, understands value-oriented infrastructure buying motions, and can translate market needs into clear product and go-to-market recommendations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Focused on the outbound phases of targeted commercial systems initiatives, this role works across stakeholders to shape market-facing strategy, offer construction, and execution without owning the core hardware roadmap, engineering backlog, factory optimization, or broader operational processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect Outbound Market Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Help shape outbound product strategy for targeted systems offerings, including product-market fit, portfolio role, initial offer hypotheses, and alternative packaging approaches for target segments to ensure strong go-to-market performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Cross-Functional Offer Construction:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the bridge between customer-facing teams and core product stakeholders, aligning technical capabilities with commercial opportunities by partnering cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Supply Chain, Customer Experience, Finance, Sales, Marketing, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Support and Service Packaging:&lt;/strong&gt; Help shape support models and services packaging, including net-new support offers where appropriate, while analyzing tradeoffs across customer adoption, support complexity, pricing, margin, and portfolio fit to deliver clear recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate Field &amp;amp; Channel Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape field and channel plays, including messaging frameworks, packaging clarity, qualification guidance, and seller enablement for target commercial segments to maximize launch execution velocity and infrastructure positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize Business Performance &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Track key business OKRs, operating metrics, and initiative performance; lead recurring cross-functional reviews to surface risks, resolve critical tradeoffs, and establish strategic plans that balance market opportunity with operational scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Infrastructure &amp;amp; Systems Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Wide-ranging experience in product management or related technical roles across enterprise infrastructure, systems, storage, servers, appliance-based infrastructure, edge systems, or adjacent technology markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-To-Market &amp;amp; Portfolio Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Full understanding of product management fundamentals, with demonstrated capabilities bringing infrastructure offerings to market through targeted segmentation, value-oriented configuration, pricing strategies, launch execution, and field/seller enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence &amp;amp; Strategic Evaluation:&lt;/strong&gt; Wide experience evaluating portfolio fit, support implications, and commercialization tradeoffs while independently managing complex design matters and coordinating across diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Discretion &amp;amp; Scheduling Initiative:&lt;/strong&gt; Seasoned professionalism in analyzing situational data to resolve variable roadmap factors, where failure to execute carefully may critically impact division goals, cost structures, or overall schedule commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
