&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiting Coordinator (AMER/Santa Clara, CA) 12 month Contract&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In Person in Santa Clara, CA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Recruiting Coordinator will play a critical role in facilitating complex, high-touch recruitment processes, serving as a pillar of support for our global talent acquisition efforts. Beyond managing day-to-day coordination, the ideal candidate will operate with a high degree of judgment and nuance, leading complex scheduling logistics, and partnering cross-functionally to optimize our operations. The ideal candidate will have excellent communication skills, be proficient in managing multiple tasks simultaneously, and demonstrate a strong ability to collaborate across diverse internal and external networks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SHOULD YOU ACCEPT THIS CHALLENGE...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage complex interview scheduling process, acting as the central point of coordination for standard, high-volume, and executive-level loops, including multi-location and international panels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate global logistics independently, proactively anticipating and resolving pitfalls such as time-zone mismatches, visa/travel conflicts, or last-minute interviewer no-shows with minimal disruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and extend offer letters and new hire paperwork, ensuring absolute accuracy, data privacy compliance within the ATS, and a seamless transition to onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process optimization by partnering with Recruiting Ops, HR, and IT to identify process gaps and implement scalable improvements that enhance the candidate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and refine team documentation, developing SOPs, scheduling templates, and checklists to increase overall team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invest in your fellow coordinators, actively leading onboarding, shadowing support, and sharing best practices during team syncs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and support marquee recruiting events, such as career fairs and campus recruiting, to help attract top talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Will work in person M-F from our Santa Clara, CA campus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL NEED TO BRING TO THIS ROLE...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of recruiting coordination, executive administration, or related fast-paced operations experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of international logistics and regional hiring norms, with proven experience coordinating across multiple regions and departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational skills and meticulous attention to detail, with a demonstrated ability to manage high-volume, shifting priorities independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS) and virtual interview tools (e.g., Google Calendar, GoodTime, Zoom), with the ability to troubleshoot system issues and support others in using them effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, with the discretion and professionalism required to partner with executives, Recruiting Ops, and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
