&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineering Manager on the Control Plane team at Everpure, you will lead a high-performing engineering team responsible for the software that manages, configures, and helps manage our hyperscale storage systems that operate at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be both a technical leader and a people manager—guiding architecture, execution, and team development across a control-plane stack built around stable APIs, predictable workflows, idempotent operations, and resilient distributed services. You will work closely with product, architecture, systems, hardware, observability, QE, release, and customer-facing teams to translate roadmap and PRD requirements into high-quality production software.&amp;nbsp;This is a role for someone who can connect technical depth with organizational leverage: building a strong team, making sound architectural decisions, driving execution through ambiguity, and improving how complex systems are operated and debugged in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a strong engineering team responsible for control-plane software, including hiring, onboarding, coaching, performance management, and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction and drive execution for control-plane investments spanning orchestration, lifecycle workflows, service interfaces, platform behavior, customer/operator experience, and operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the architecture and development of robust, scalable services in Go and related infrastructure, with strong emphasis on correctness, debuggability, maintainability, and operational resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Management and Architecture to translate PRD and customer requirements into concrete control-plane capabilities such as local and automated management flows, runbook-friendly interfaces, upgrade and rollback behavior, readiness checks, and safe control over platform operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster strong engineering practices including design reviews, code reviews, automated testing, CI/CD discipline, observability, and clear operational ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an environment of accountability, urgency, and psychological safety where engineers can do their best work and grow in scope over time.We are primarily an in-office environment and therefore, you will be expected to work from the Santa Clara office in compliance with Everpure&#39;s policies, unless you are on PTO, or work travel, or other approved leave.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of engineering management experience, with a strong track record of leading software teams and developing engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering experience building production systems, infrastructure software, control software, or distributed services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical depth in distributed systems, backend platforms, infrastructure software, or cloud-native architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding architecture and execution for systems that require strong reliability, recoverability, operator clarity, and safe behavior under failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Go (preferred) or comparable backend/systems technologies, plus the ability to guide high-quality implementation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience balancing feature delivery with technical debt, quality, security, and supportability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to influence across teams, functions, and levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
