&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure is standing up a dedicated Supply Planning function from scratch, and this role gets to help build it. You&#39;ll own end-to-end supply planning for a product platform while helping shape the team&#39;s operating cadence, SOPs, and tools as one of its founding members — and you&#39;ll lead the shift from a finished-goods buffer strategy to Configure-to-Order (CTO), including attach-rate-driven planning for accessories and semi-finished goods. You&#39;ll work closely with contract manufacturing partners on the ground and serve as the key supply planning voice in our SAP IBP and S/4HANA transformation, partnering across Demand Planning, Procurement, Manufacturing, and NPI to keep plans aligned to the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end supply planning for your platform, translating demand signals into executable build, capacity, and material plans across internal and CM sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the transition from finished-goods buffer to Configure-to-Order for your platform, including buffer positioning and attach rate models for accessories and semi-finished goods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary supply planning point of contact for your assigned contract manufacturer(s), driving planning cycles, capacity commitments, and performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the business SME for supply planning in the SAP IBP/S/4HANA implementation — shaping requirements, process design, and driving adoption to close gaps between current tooling and the CTO model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the Supply Planning function itself: contribute to its SOPs, KPIs, and playbook as the team scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on supply planning experience in high-tech or electronics manufacturing, with fluency in Configure-to-Order processes and multi-level BOM management, including buffer positioning and safety stock methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct, hands-on experience planning in SAP (MM/PP/APO) along with SAP IBP or an equivalent APS platform (o9, Kinaxis, Blue Yonder)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing capacity, allocation, and planning cadence directly with contract manufacturers or EMS partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort contributing to ERP/APS implementations, including documenting business requirements, plus the cross-functional influence to align demand planning, sourcing, and execution partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data fluency — advanced Excel/analysis skills and the ability to build structure into large, imperfect datasets in an ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are primarily an in-office environment&lt;/strong&gt; and therefore, you will be expected to work from the &lt;strong&gt;Santa Clara, CA&lt;/strong&gt; office in compliance with Everpure&#39;s policies, unless you are on PTO, or work travel, or other approved leave.&lt;/p&gt;
